11
00:47:15,555 --> 00:47:21,555
Let Me In is a 2010 romantic horror film written and directed by Matt Reeves.

12
00:51:33,333 --> 00:51:39,333
It is a remake of the 2008 Swedish film Let the Right One In, which was based
on the 2004 novel of the same name by John Ajvide Lindqvist.

13
00:55:51,111 --> 00:55:57,111
The film stars Kodi Smit-McPhee, Chloë Grace Moretz,
Elias Koteas, and Richard Jenkins.

14
01:00:08,888 --> 01:00:14,888
The plot follows a bullied 12-year-old boy who befriends and develops a romantic relationship
with a child vampire girl in Los Alamos, New Mexico, during the early 1980s.

15
01:04:26,666 --> 01:04:32,666
Interest in producing an English-language version of Let the Right One In
began in 2007, shortly before the Swedish film was released.

16
01:08:44,444 --> 01:08:50,444
In 2008, Hammer Films acquired the rights for the English adaptation and initially offered Tomas
Alfredson, the director of the original film, the opportunity to direct, which he declined.

17
01:13:02,222 --> 01:13:08,222
Reeves was then signed to direct and write the screenplay.

18
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
Reeves made several changes for the English version, such as altering the setting
from Stockholm to Los Alamos and renaming the lead characters.

19
01:21:37,777 --> 01:21:43,777
The film's producers stated that their intent was to keep the plot similar to
the original, yet make it more accessible to a wider audience.

20
01:25:55,555 --> 01:26:01,555
Principal photography began in early November
2009 and concluded in January 2010.

21
01:30:13,333 --> 01:30:19,333
Let Me In premiered at the 2010 Toronto International Film Festival on September 13, 2010, and was released in the United
States on October 1, by Overture Films, and in the United Kingdom on November 5, by Icon Film Distribution.

22
01:34:31,111 --> 01:34:37,111
The film received positive reviews from critics, being placed on
several top ten lists of best films of the year.

23
01:38:48,888 --> 01:38:54,888
Many critics noted it as a rare English-language remake which stayed true to the original,
while others criticized it for being too derivative of the Swedish film.

24
01:43:06,666 --> 01:43:12,666
It earned $27 million worldwide against a production budget of $20 million.

25
01:47:24,444 --> 01:47:30,444
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
vampire, bullying, bully, child vampire.

26
01:51:42,222 --> 01:51:48,222
The tone is dark and emotional and mind_bending.
